---
id: org.dxos.plugin.readwise
name: ReadwisePlugin
version: 0.1.0
---

Connects a Readwise account into Composer. Steve saves articles, PDFs, and videos to Readwise/Reader
and highlights passages with notes; this plugin connects the account, syncs those highlights in, and
lets Steve browse them grouped by source — ready to reference alongside everything else in the
workspace.

This is the first increment of a larger arc — the horizontal **Workbench** (see
`docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-06-workbench-concept.md`), which Readwise merely feeds: connect, sync,
and browse only — everything past browsing (triage / AI / work / connect) is reserved for later
Workbench increments. No new
ECHO types are introduced beyond the
plugin's own `Readwise` (account) and `Highlight` (annotation) objects; everything else composes
`Bookmark`, `Connection`, `AccessToken`, `Cursor`, and `SyncBinding` (all reused as-is from
`@dxos/types`, `@dxos/echo`, `@dxos/plugin-bookmarks`, `@dxos/plugin-connector`).

## Extensions

The following extension dialects are used in this document.
Each extension is defined in the Appendix or resolved via its URI.

| Term        | URI                            |
|-------------|--------------------------------|
| `type`      | `org.dxos.mdl.type@1.0`       |
| `feat`      | `org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0`       |
| `test`      | `org.dxos.mdl.test@1.0`       |
| `component` | `org.dxos.mdl.component@1.0`  |
| `op`        | `org.dxos.mdl.op@1.0`         |
| `service`   | `org.dxos.mdl.service@1.0`    |

## Types

```mdl
type Highlight
  desc: One Readwise highlight or synthetic document-note annotation, decoded from the wire response.
  fields:
    readwiseId: string
    text: string          # empty for a synthetic document-note annotation
    note: string
    tags: string[]
    location?: number
    url?: string
    updated: string        # ISO timestamp, the per-item high-water mark
    sourceTitle: string
    sourceAuthor?: string
    sourceUrl?: string
    sourceCategory?: string
    sourceImage?: string
    sourceId: string       # stable per-document id; the Bookmark dedup key
    sourceUniqueUrl?: string
```

```mdl
type CaptureResult
  fields:
    created: number
    updated: number
```

## Services

```mdl
service ReadwiseApi
  desc: |
    Authenticated REST client for the Readwise v2 highlights export API,
    reachable via an injectable Transport (direct | vite-proxy | edge-proxy —
    defaulting to the shared EDGE CORS proxy in the browser). Decodes the wire
    response into Highlight, synthesizing one document-note Highlight (empty
    text) per document that has a note but no highlights.
  ops:
    listHighlightsSince(updatedAfter?: string) → ListHighlightsResult
  effects: [http]
  errors:
    ReadwiseError: request failed or returned an unexpected payload
```

## Operations

```mdl
op captureHighlights
  desc: |
    Idempotently captures a batch of Highlight as ECHO objects into one connected
    Readwise account: one Bookmark per distinct source document, one Highlight
    object per annotation (referencing its Bookmark and the account). Re-running
    with the same (or a superset of) highlights creates no duplicates; a
    highlight whose note changed updates the existing object in place.
  input:
    highlights: Highlight[]
  output: CaptureResult
  effects: [echo:write]
```

```mdl
op ReadwiseOperation.Sync
  desc: |
    Reconciles Readwise highlights for one connected account: resolves the
    account's Connection for credentials, pulls every highlight updated since
    the account's cursor (or since a default recent window on the very first
    run, rather than the entire library), captures them via captureHighlights,
    then advances the cursor to the run-start timestamp on success (or records
    the failure on the cursor, leaving the cursor value untouched, on failure).
    Pull-only and idempotent — matches the Connector.sync contract so it is
    wired as a ConnectorEntry.sync operation, and is also triggered directly by
    the account's own "Sync" affordance and automatically once, right after the
    account is first connected.
  input:
    binding: Ref<SyncBinding>
  output: CaptureResult
  effects: [echo:read, echo:write, http]
```

```mdl
op ReadwiseOperation.MaterializeTarget
  desc: Creates the Readwise account container for a new connection, invoked by the Connector framework when connecting without an existing target.
  output: Readwise
  effects: [echo:write]
```

## Components

```mdl
component ReadwiseContainer
  desc: |
    Main article surface for a Readwise account. Unconnected, renders a
    "Connect Readwise" affordance instead of a blank pane. Connected, renders a
    "Sync" action and the account's highlights grouped by source document,
    most-recently-active source first. Auto-runs one sync immediately after the
    account is first connected.
  props:
    subject: Readwise
    attendableId?: string
  actions:
    sync() → CaptureResult
  layout: |
    ┌─────────────────────────────────────┐
    │                            [Sync]   │
    ├─────────────────────────────────────┤
    │ Source A · 2                        │
    │  [highlight card]                   │
    │  [highlight card]                   │
    ├─────────────────────────────────────┤
    │ Source B · 1                        │
    │  [highlight card]                   │
    └─────────────────────────────────────┘
```

```mdl
component HighlightCard
  desc: |
    One highlight's card within the grouped browse view: the passage, the note
    when present, and tags. Also renders an inert (reserved, non-functional)
    processing-state indicator and an inert "where it's processed" affordance —
    placeholders a later increment activates. Opens the highlight's detail view
    when clicked or activated via keyboard.
  props:
    subject: Highlight
```

```mdl
component HighlightDetail
  desc: Full detail for one highlight — the complete passage, the note, tags, and a link to the source document.
  props:
    subject: Highlight
```

## Features

```mdl
feat F-1: Create and Connect

  req F-1.1:
    given: a space with no Readwise account
    when: the user creates one from the "+ Add" menu
    then: a Readwise account is created and opens

  req F-1.2:
    given: a Readwise account with no connection
    when: the user opens it
    then: a "Connect Readwise" affordance is shown, not a blank pane

  req F-1.3:
    given: a Readwise account with no connection
    when: the user enters a valid Readwise API token
    then: the account is connected without any OAuth step
    and: the first sync begins automatically
```

```mdl
feat F-2: Browse

  req F-2.1:
    given: a connected Readwise account with synced highlights
    when: the user views it
    then: highlights appear grouped under their source document
    and: the most-recently-active source is listed first
    and: each card shows the passage, the note when present, and tags
    and: each card renders an inert processing-state indicator and an inert "where it's processed" affordance

  req F-2.2:
    given: a highlight card
    when: the user opens it
    then: the full passage, the note, and a link to the source document are shown
```

```mdl
feat F-3: Sync

  req F-3.1:
    given: a connected Readwise account
    when: the user invokes the "Sync" action
    then: new and changed highlights are pulled in
    and: nothing already present is duplicated
    and: a source that gains a highlight moves to the top of the browse view

  req F-3.2:
    given: a Readwise account connecting for the first time
    when: its first sync runs
    then: only a default recent window of history is pulled, not the entire library
```

## Acceptance

```mdl
test T-1: Capture is idempotent
  desc: Automated — src/operations/capture.test.ts.
  given: a connected Readwise account with synced highlights
  when: sync runs again with no new remote activity
  then:
    - each highlight still appears exactly once
    - no duplicate objects are created
    - a highlight whose note changed is updated in place rather than duplicated
```

```mdl
test T-2: Browse groups by source, most-recent first
  desc: Automated — src/operations/browse-query.test.ts.
  given: synced highlights spanning several source documents with different last-activity times
  when: the browse view is computed
  then: highlights are grouped by their source document
  and: the groups are ordered by that source's most recent activity, newest first
```

```mdl
test T-3: Connect form validates and builds a connection
  desc: Automated — src/capabilities/readwise-credential-form.test.ts.
  given: the "Connect Readwise" form
  then:
    - submitting an empty token is rejected
    - submitting a valid token produces a working connection, with no OAuth step
```

```mdl
test T-4: Sync captures and advances the cursor, bounded by a default window on first run
  desc: Automated — src/operations/sync.test.ts.
  given: a newly connected account with no prior sync
  when: sync runs, then runs again
  then:
    - the first run only pulls history back to a default recent window, not the entire library
    - the first run creates the synced highlights and their source documents
    - the second run creates nothing new
    - the account's high-water mark advances after the first run
```

```mdl
test T-5: Walking-skeleton acceptance — create, connect, browse, open
  desc: Covered by the live manual acceptance run against a running Composer, not a unit test.
  given: a space with no Readwise account
  when: the user creates one, connects it with a real token, and browses and opens its highlights
  then:
    - creating from "+ Add" opens the account
    - the unconnected account shows "Connect Readwise", not a blank pane
    - a valid token connects without OAuth and the first sync runs automatically
    - highlights appear grouped by source, most-recently-active source first
    - re-running "Sync" pulls changes without duplicating anything
    - opening a highlight shows its full passage, note, and a link to its source
```

